content:
Use coordinates with the bottom-left corner as \((0,0)\). The beam starts at \((2,0)\) moving upward.

Its reflections are:
\[
(2,0)\uparrow
\to(2,2)\text{ on a }\backslash\text{ mirror}\to\text{left}
\]
\[
\to(1,2)\to\text{up}
\to(1,3)\text{ on a }/\text{ mirror}\to\text{right}
\]
\[
\to(2,3)\to\text{down}
\to(2,2)\to\text{right}
\]
\[
\to(3,2)\to\text{down}
\to(3,1)\to\text{right}
\]
\[
\to(4,1)\to\text{down}.
\]
The beam then reaches the bottom edge at \((4,0)\), which is labeled \(C\).

\[
\boxed{\text{C}}
\]
